CLASS:: MultirateOctaveShift
summary:: Cascaded multirate filterbank octave shifter
categories:: UGens>Pitch
related:: Guides/PitchShiftSuite, Classes/ERBPhaseOctave, Classes/SubbandPhaseHalf

DESCRIPTION::
MultirateOctaveShift is an octave shifter using cascaded multirate half-band decimation and interpolation filtering. By splitting the signal into octave frequency registers, it transposes audio up (+1 octave) or down (-1 octave) without phase vocoding or grain splicing artifacts, maintaining clean transient response and transparent harmonic balance.

Processing is monophonic; multichannel expansion applies over Arrays. Supports sample rates from 44.1 kHz to 96 kHz (calibrated at 48 kHz).

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar

ARGUMENT:: in
Audio-rate mono input signal.

ARGUMENT:: voice
Octave voice selection (scalar: 0 = +1 octave up, 1 = -1 octave down). Default is 0.

returns:: An audio-rate pitch-shifted signal.

EXAMPLES::

SUBSECTION:: Synthetic Signals

code::
// 1. Monophonic Sine: plays original (220 Hz) then pitch-shifted (voice 0: +1 octave)
(
fork {
    // Original
    x = {
        var sig = SinOsc.ar(220, 0, 0.1);
        sig * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
    2.1.wait;

    // Pitch-shifted
    x = {
        var sig = SinOsc.ar(220, 0, 0.1);
        var shifted = MultirateOctaveShift.ar(sig, 0);
        shifted * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
};
)

// 2. Polyphonic Chord: plays original chord then pitch-shifted
(
fork {
    // Original chord
    x = {
        var sig = Mix(SinOsc.ar([220, 277.18, 329.63], 0, 0.05));
        sig * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
    2.1.wait;

    // Pitch-shifted chord
    x = {
        var sig = Mix(SinOsc.ar([220, 277.18, 329.63], 0, 0.05));
        var shifted = MultirateOctaveShift.ar(sig, 0);
        shifted * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
};
)

// 3. Percussive / Transient: plays original bursts then pitch-shifted
(
fork {
    // Original bursts
    x = {
        var sig = PinkNoise.ar(0.1) * Decay2.ar(Impulse.ar(4), 0.005, 0.15);
        sig * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
    2.1.wait;

    // Pitch-shifted bursts
    x = {
        var sig = PinkNoise.ar(0.1) * Decay2.ar(Impulse.ar(4), 0.005, 0.15);
        var shifted = MultirateOctaveShift.ar(sig, 0);
        shifted * EnvGen.kr(Env.linen(0.05, 1.9, 0.05), doneAction: 2) ! 2;
    }.play;
};
)
::

SUBSECTION:: Recorded Audio

code::
// 4. Monophonic Recorded Sound (Guitar): original, then pitch-shifted
(
fork {
    var buf = Buffer.read(s, Platform.userExtensionDir +/+ "PitchShiftSuite/HelpSource/Audio/PitchShiftSuite/guitar-monophonic.wav");
    s.sync;

    // Original
    x = { PlayBuf.ar(1, buf, BufRateScale.kr(buf), doneAction: 2) ! 2 }.play;
    buf.duration.wait;

    // Pitch-shifted
    x = {
        var sig = PlayBuf.ar(1, buf, BufRateScale.kr(buf), doneAction: 2);
        MultirateOctaveShift.ar(sig, 0) ! 2;
    }.play;
    (buf.duration + 0.2).wait;

    buf.free;
};
)

// 5. Polyphonic Recorded Sound (Piano Chords): original, then pitch-shifted
(
fork {
    var buf = Buffer.read(s, Platform.userExtensionDir +/+ "PitchShiftSuite/HelpSource/Audio/PitchShiftSuite/piano-polyphonic.wav");
    s.sync;

    // Original
    x = { PlayBuf.ar(1, buf, BufRateScale.kr(buf), doneAction: 2) ! 2 }.play;
    buf.duration.wait;

    // Pitch-shifted
    x = {
        var sig = PlayBuf.ar(1, buf, BufRateScale.kr(buf), doneAction: 2);
        MultirateOctaveShift.ar(sig, 1) ! 2;
    }.play;
    (buf.duration + 0.2).wait;

    buf.free;
};
)
::
